/* book exam traps: Smoke detection is not suppression. A cargo smoke warning starts the chain; the bottles do the extinguishing. | On fire-handle types the handle has two actions: pulling isolates and arms, rotating discharges. Writing only "pull to discharge" loses marks. | A squib is one-shot. A test does not fire the squib; it only tests the circuit. | Halon 1301 does not work mainly by removing oxygen. It breaks the chemical chain, so a low concentration can stop a flame. | Dual loops in AND logic need both loops to warn; that cuts false alarms, and a failed loop is dropped automatically with a FAULT light, so writing "one loop must fail before the other works" is wrong. */
